# mkrisher's dot-files

My macOS setup, declared as a Nix flake: [nix-darwin](https://github.com/nix-darwin/nix-darwin) for the system and Homebrew, [home-manager](https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager) for dotfile symlinks, and [devenv](https://devenv.sh) for per-project languages and gems.

I use Neovim (LazyVim), Zsh with Starship, tmux and Zellij.

## Setup

Requires Nix (Determinate installer) and Homebrew.

```
git clone https://github.com/mkrisher/dotfiles.git ~/projects/dotfiles
cd ~/projects/dotfiles

# first time only
sudo nix run nix-darwin -- switch --flake .#Mike-M5

# afterwards
sudo darwin-rebuild switch --flake ~/projects/dotfiles
```

## Layout

- `flake.nix`: inputs and the `Mike-M5` machine
- `nix/darwin.nix`: system settings and fonts
- `nix/homebrew.nix`: Homebrew taps, formulae and casks. Add packages here.
- `nix/home.nix`: dotfile symlinks, home-manager packages (devenv, direnv, tmuxinator) and setup steps
- `config/`: the dotfiles themselves, symlinked into place by `nix/home.nix`

Dotfiles are symlinked to this checkout rather than copied, so edits take effect without a rebuild.

## Languages

Ruby, Node and Rust live in each project's `devenv.nix`. Projects opt in with a `.envrc` containing `eval "$(devenv direnvrc)" && use devenv`. Python is installed with `uv`.

## PARA

I use the PARA method for organizing my files: Projects, Areas, Resources and Archives directories. Look up Building A Second Brain if you are not familiar.
